/*
 * Declares the NullValue class.
 *
 * NullValue represents the literal `null`, which is a pointer value with no
 * associated address. It may be typed or untyped:
 *
 *   - A typed null has an explicit PointerType.
 *   - An untyped null is implicitly castable to any pointer type.
 *
 * NullValue is always a full literal, always reduced, immutable, and never an
 * lvalue. It participates in compile-time evaluation and is used wherever a null
 * pointer literal is required.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::literal::null_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/literal/null_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
